ADDITIONAL NOTICE: CHILD-SAFETY PRODUCT

This is a child-safety product. The target user population includes children
between 3 and 12 years of age. Production deployments that process real
child data MUST independently satisfy, in addition to the MIT license
terms above:

  (a) A signed Parental Consent record under applicable law (e.g. COPPA in
      the US, GDPR-K in the EU).
  (b) A region-specific Privacy Policy presented to and acknowledged by the
      parent at sign-up.
  (c) A documented Data Deletion workflow capable of completing within the
      window required by applicable law (Niki's design target is 30 days; your
      mileage may vary).
  (d) An independent Security review of the four-tier privacy classifier and
      the AES-256-GCM treehole encryption module.
  (e) Local regulatory compliance signed off by qualified counsel.

The MIT license does not, and is not intended to, waive any of the above
obligations. The Authors make this Software available primarily for review,
education, and integration testing. The Authors have not authorised any
deployment of this Software to real child users; any such deployment is at
the deployer's sole risk and responsibility.
